    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nIs it possible to populate the quickfix list with the matching files from mini.pick?\r\n\r\nMy typical workflow with Telescope was to grep for a given string, populate the quickfix list using `<C-q>`, and then run `:cfdo` on the matching files. It's a very convenient way to perform project-wide changes.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is it possible to populate the quickfix list with the matching files from mini.pick?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My typical workflow with Telescope was to grep for a given string, populate the quickfix list using <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-q&gt;</code>, and then run <code class=\"notranslate\">:cfdo</code> on the matching files. It's a very convenient way to perform project-wide changes.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nIs it possible to populate the quickfix list with the matching files from mini.pick?\nMy typical workflow with Telescope was to grep for a given string, populate the quickfix list using <C-q>, and then run :cfdo on the matching files. It's a very convenient way to perform project-wide changes.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
